  "id": "lateral-olfactory-tract",
  "term": "lateral olfactory tract",
  "definition": "The lateral olfactory tract is a pathway formed by axons from mitral cells that carries smell-related information toward the cerebral cortex, including the piriform cortex. Its normal development and positioning are important for proper innervation of olfactory cortical areas.",
